  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 329 AM EDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nThe ridge is finally expected to break down Sunday night into \nMonday as another front approaches from the Mid MS river valley. \nIsolated thunderstorms become more widespread beginning Monday \nafternoon. We'll see storm chances between 50% and 75% through \nTuesday before another ridge turns the flow more NW and we get cut\noff from the Gulf moisture towards late part of the work week. \n\nThis will help to moderate temps down to the upper 80s and low 90s \nby Wednesday and settle into the mid to low 80s towards the end of \nnext week as the dry air clears out afternoon convection chances. \nLow Temps will drop back into 60s Wednesday night into Thursday and \nwe'll get a pleasant taste of fall.",
